pe":"Original","name":"Manticore's Badge","stages":[]},{"type":"Upgrade","name":"AMB-X: Tail-Protection Training Tool","mission":{"requirement1":"Complete a total of 5 battles; You must deploy your own Manticore, and unleash Toxic Overload at least 1 time in each battle","requirement2":"Clear Main Theme 1-9 with a 3-star rating; You must deploy your own Manticore, and can only include 1 other Operator as a member"},"stages":[{"stage":"Stage 1","attributesIncreased":"ATK +58 , DEF +22","effectLabel":"New trait","effectText":"Slows the Movement Speed of enemies within this unit's Attack Range by 20%","cost":[{"name":"Module Data Block","quantity":2},{"name":"Cutting Fluid Solution","quantity":3},{"name":"LMD","quantity":40000}]},{"stage":"Stage 2","attributesIncreased":"ATK +72 , DEF +27","effectLabel":"Hidden Killer - Elite improved","effectText":"Stays Invisible normally. The first attack made gains +55% ATK and removes Invisibility . Regains Invisible state after not attacking for 5 seconds","cost":[{"name":"Module Data Block","quantity":2},{"name":"Data Supplement Stick","quantity":20},{"name":"Keton Colloid","quantity":4},{"name":"LMD","quantity":50000}]},{"stage":"Stage 3","attributesIncreased":"ATK +85 , DEF +31","effectLabel":"Hidden Killer - Elite improved","effectText":"Stays Invisible normally. The first attack made gains +60% ATK and removes Invisibility . Regains Invisible state after not attacking for 5 seconds","cost":[{"name":"Module Data Block","quantity":2},{"name":"Data Supplement Instrument","quantity":8},{"name":"Sugar Lump","quantity":5},{"name":"LMD","quantity":60000}]}]}],"review":{"official":"Much of Manticore's history is unknown. It is known that prior to her employment at\nRhodes Island\n, she had engaged in the \"removal\" of others. She has excellent stealth, infiltration, and surprise attack skills.\nNow she is a special kind of\nOperator\nwho provides these special services for Rhodes Island.","editor":null,"rating":null},"synergies":[],"techniques":[{"technique":null,"techniqueDescription":null,"description":null}],"guides":[],"stats":{"phases":[{"elite":0,"minLevel":1,"maxLevel":50,"base":{"hp":777,"atk":378,"def":141,"res":10,"redeploy":70,"dp":18,"block":0,"interval":3.5},"max":{"hp":1080,"atk":511,"def":218,"res":10,"redeploy":70,"dp":18,"block":0,"interval":3.5},"rangeId":"y-1"},{"elite":1,"minLevel":1,"maxLevel":70,"base":{"hp":1080,"atk":511,"def":218,"res":20,"redeploy":70,"dp":20,"block":0,"interval":3.5},"max":{"hp":1385,"atk":656,"def":284,"res":20,"redeploy":70,"dp":20,"block":0,"interval":3.5},"rangeId":"y-1"},{"elite":2,"minLevel":1,"maxLevel":80,"base":{"hp":1385,"atk":656,"def":284,"res":30,"redeploy":70,"dp":20,"block":0,"interval":3.5},"max":{"hp":1630,"atk":811,"def":343,"res":30,"redeploy":70,"dp":20,"block":0,"interval":3.5},"rangeId":"y-1"}],"trust":{"hp":0,"atk":60,"def":30}},"files":[{"section":"Clinical Analysis","unlock":"Unlocked at 25 trust","description":"Imaging tests have shown the outlines of her internal organs to be indistinct due to abnormal shadows. Originium granules have been detected in her circulatory system, confirming her to be infected with Oripathy.\n\n[Cell-Originium Assimilation] 12% \nOperator has no obvious ore lesions on the surface of her body. Tests have revealed the presence of crystals internally, however. \n\n[Blood Originium-Crystal Density] 0.32u/L \nDue to the presence of Originium within the Operator's internal organs, the Operator's shows an elevated blood crystal content."},{"section":"Archive File 1","unlock":"Unlocked at 50 trust","description":"Manticore is gentle, shy, and sometimes even gives others the feeling that she's afraid. She speaks in a hesitant tone and often stammers. She rarely finishes a sentence in one attempt, and she appears very stiff when communicating with other Operators. She would probably be more comfortable talking to a rock.\nAdditionally, her rare invisibility ability has become a major hindrance to communication. It has completely prevented her from improving her interpersonal skills. It may be necessary to suggest additional treatment solutions to help Manticore develop her social skills."},{"section":"Archive File 2","unlock":"Unlocked at 100 trust","description":"We communicate with Manticore by writing messages on paper. Oripathy has given her the ability to turn invisible (the report on this ability needs additional processing). It has been confirmed through interactive experiments that her ability does not transfer to inanimate objects, so paper communication has proved a suitable way to communicate with this operator.\nAfter communication, Manticore likes to leave behind little gifts that smell sweetly of violets."},{"section":"Archive File 3","unlock":"Unlocked at 150 trust","description":"Manticore was born in Sargon. Because most of the background she provided could not be validated, Manticore's experience cannot be confirmed. What is known is that Manticore has undergone relatively comprehensive special operations training and has at least one year of operative experience under her belt.\nThe investigation into her special operations training unit was unsuccessful, and Sargon intelligence did not provide any valuable clues. Currently only unconfirmed and less than reliable intelligence from Sargon spies indicate there is a group of people who house Originium Arts users with special abilities in this area. These individuals are using special training methods to kill Sargon aristocrats or operatives from other nations.\nBecause of Manticore's vague background, she has been designated a special type of Oripathy patient at Rhodes Island. Any applications requesting use of Manticore in special operations or combat will first need to be submitted to Dr. Kal'tsit for approval."},{"section":"Archive File 4","unlock":"Unlocked at 200 trust","description":"[Manticore's Ability's Test Record] \nTest subject: Manticore. \nTest objective: To probe the usefulness of the subject's abilities and Originium Arts. \nTest content: To find Manticore while she is in hiding and to defend against her while she is in action. \nTest participants: An Operator who has worked with Manticore on several missions. \nRandomly select two Operators from all of the Operators available. \nAmong them must be at least one technician Operator or non-technician Operator with high Originium adaptability. \nTest results: The test took place on a terrain simulating a complex environment. During the test period, none of the three Operators were able to locate the whereabouts of Manticore. When Manticore went on the offensive, some of the Operators managed to defend against her attacks using their quick reaction times and combat experience, while Manticore managed to successfully attack the others. \nFeedback results: According to the explanations provided by the Operators, Manticore could not be captured using visual means. Some of the Operators with better Originium adaptability reported feeling a strange atmosphere that instantly made them as though they were in danger. \nThe above process has been recorded in its entirety. If you wish to view it, you must request it from the relevant department."}]},"appearances":[{"label":"Base","iconPath":"/five-star-icons/Manticore%20-%20Base.webp","fullPath":"/five-star-skins/Manticore%20-%20Base.webp"},{"label":"Elite 2","iconPath":"/five-star-icons/Manticore%20-%20Elite%202.webp","fullPath":"/five-star-skins/Manticore%20-%20Elite%202.webp"},{"label":"Invisible Dirge","iconPath":"/five-star-icons/Manticore%20-%20Invisible%20Dirge.webp","fullPath":"/five-star-skins/Manticore%20-%20Invisible%20Dirge.webp"},{"label":"Under A Veil","iconPath":"/five-star-icons/Manticore%20-%20Under%20A%20Veil.webp","fullPath":"/five-star-skins/Manticore%20-%20Under%20A%20Veil.webp"}],"skinObtainByLabel":{"Invisible Dirge":"40 DC / 400 UC","Under A Veil":"18 OP"},"synergyMatches":[],"autoSynergyGroups":[{"name":"Sargon","type":"faction","entr